    out=run(s+"\n", args=["-H",str(H)] if H!=1.0 else [])
    print(f"s={repr(s):8} H={H} sim {repr(sim):10} {[hex(ord(c)-0x2800) for c in sim]} vs out {repr(out):10} {[hex(ord(c)-0x2800) for c in out]} equal {sim==out}")

# Need to also handle leading blanks: w includes leading blanks, but our filled check p>=first ensures leading blanks not filled. However n_scaled includes leading blanks as well (since w includes them). For "  a" w=3 first2, n_scaled ceil3*0.5=2 => scaled cols 0,1. p=2 interval [1.0,1.5) center1.5 => sp1 filled => would give scaled col1 filled, but our earlier simulation predicted sp1 for "  a" H0.5 would be right dot but observed blank. Let's see what our new center model gives for "  a" H0.5.

